ry>This frozen mac and cheese I got one time is labeled as having 2.5 255 gram servings in a box of 567 grams total. Interesting.</summary> </entry> <entry><title>N-M Balancers from 2-2 Balancers</title><link href="https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/n-m-balancers/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="N-M Balancers from 2-2 Balancers" /><published>2026-11-04T00:00:00-08:00</published> <updated>2026-11-06T14:39:33-08:00</updated> <id>https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/n-m-balancers/</id> <content type="text/html" src="https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/n-m-balancers/" /> <author> <name>Mikel Mcdaniel</name> </author> <category term="Math" /> <category term="CS" /> <summary>An N-M balancer is something that has N inputs and M outputs. Whatever goes into 1 input is evenly balanced among the M outputs. What's the minimum number of 2-2 balancers needed to make an N-M balancer?</summary> </entry> <entry><title>Split Computation on Rings</title><link href="https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/split-ring-computation/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Split Computation on Rings" /><published>2026-09-30T00:00:00-07:00</published> <updated>2026-11-06T14:39:33-08:00</updated> <id>https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/split-ring-computation/</id> <content type="text/html" src="https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/split-ring-computation/" /> <author> <name>Mikel Mcdaniel</name> </author> <category term="Math" /> <category term="CS" /> <summary>Breaking apart arithmetic on non-negative integers for bogus speed and security benefits and maybe something actually practical.</summary> </entry> <entry><title>I love my BF Challenges at BSidesSF 2026</title><link href="https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/i-love-my-bf-bsides-ctf/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="I love my BF Challenges at BSidesSF 2026" /><published>2026-03-22T00:00:00-07:00</published> <updated>2026-11-06T14:39:33-08:00</updated> <id>https://mikelmcdaniel.github.io//posts/i-love-my-b